 :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd8e6d11-24ab-54f4-9302-a197b45ae78f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252504} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e5bd1bd-eab3-5250-8633-db4827abfabb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "605f5d22-0a36-54b2-9fda-393ada9a651b" :question/math-academy-id "q-11653" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle M=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & w \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(M)=2$, what is the value of $w?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & w \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-w\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4w.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nSince $det(M)=2$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =2 \\\\ 6-4w & =2 \\\\ -4w & =2-6 \\\\ -4w & =-4 \\\\ w & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262796 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2129aee3-923d-57de-8bdc-983ffdf787f1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Integer Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78dc759e-2781-5f7c-8fdf-32c8a7488616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260936} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e65376-d802-5c70-a9b5-c7a733c9a942" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261331} {:answer/id #uuid "bb19c345-96c8-5417-8091-0779682fa6e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261521} {:answer/id #uuid "e51f0554-9934-5f77-b1d4-2f9e022ea1c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :a