"k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260279} {:answer/id #uuid "2e9b7936-2a9f-5fa6-98b8-c2d31209e615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260296} {:answer/id #uuid "6e18de3f-d88f-51e5-8a5a-4c7a07f3003b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260842} {:answer/id #uuid "72f9541a-9495-523a-a73a-4a7b746e235a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cde1f0f-ce43-5b48-8b5f-a4207965af8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260279} :answer-field/id #uuid "469de0af-655e-5c52-99af-6a01835c14fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb9b1b8a-cede-5e44-9f81-ee8a71692716" :question/math-academy-id "q-127604" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle U=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 2k & -k+2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(U)=-1$, what is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(U) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 2k & -k+2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-k+2)-(-5)\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =7k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-1$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-1 \\\\ 7k+6 & =-1 \\\\ 7k & =-1-6 \\\\ 7k & =-7 \\\\ k & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262804 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ccdde46-a4ab-517e-910b-571a3a166b6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Expression Involving the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices 